drm/etnaviv: set cmdbuf->suballoc only once the allocation succeeded

etnaviv_cmdbuf_init() stores the suballocator in the cmdbuf before it
looks for space, and submit_cleanup() takes a non-NULL cmdbuf->suballoc
to mean "this cmdbuf holds granules".  When the allocation fails in the
submit ioctl, the error path therefore calls etnaviv_cmdbuf_free() on a
cmdbuf that owns nothing.  suballoc_offset is still 0 from kzalloc(), so that
releases the granules at the start of the region, which belong to a
live buffer (the first one allocated is the GPU's own ring buffer), and
a later submit can be handed the same memory.

Today only the 10 second timeout reaches this.  Set the pointer together
with the offset, after the region has been found.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_cmdbuf.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_cmdbuf.c
@@ -87,7 +87,6 @@ int etnaviv_cmdbuf_init(struct etnaviv_c
 {
 	int granule_offs, order, ret;
 
-	cmdbuf->suballoc = suballoc;
 	cmdbuf->size = size;
 
 	order = order_base_2(ALIGN(size, SUBALLOC_GRANULE) / SUBALLOC_GRANULE);
@@ -109,6 +108,7 @@ retry:
 		goto retry;
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&suballoc->lock);
+	cmdbuf->suballoc = suballoc;
 	cmdbuf->suballoc_offset = granule_offs * SUBALLOC_GRANULE;
 	cmdbuf->vaddr = suballoc->vaddr + cmdbuf->suballoc_offset;
 
